own-body"><h1 id=3D"get-started">Get Started</h1>
<h2 id=3D"prerequisites">Prerequisites</h2>
<p>minSdkVersion 19 or higher</p>
<h2 id=3D"import-the-bigo-ads-sdk">Import the Bigo Ads SDK</h2>
<ol>
<li>
<p>In your project-level <code>build.gradle</code> file, include <a href=3D=
"https://search.maven.org/artifact">Maven central repository</a> in both yo=
ur <code>buildscript</code> and <code>allprojects</code> sections:</p>
<pre><code class=3D"hljs language-groovy">buildscript {
    repositories {
        ...
        mavenCentral()
    }
}

allprojects {
    repositories {
        ...
        mavenCentral()
    }
}
</code></pre>
</li>
<li>
<p>Add the dependencies for the Bigo Ads SDK to your module's app-level Gra=
dle file, which is usually <code>app/build.gradle</code>:</p>
<pre><code class=3D"hljs language-groovy">dependencies {
    ...
    implementation 'com.bigossp:bigo-ads:4.9.1'
}
</code></pre>
</li>
<li>
<p>Set Specific Domain ClearText. BigoAds SDK has some features to lower ad=
 latency, which could serve ads faster. To enable these features, please fo=
llow below instruction and allow 127.0.0.1 cleartext.<br>Create a file <cod=
e>res/xml/network_security_config.xml</code> in the following path with the=
 following content:</p>
<pre><code class=3D"hljs language-xml"><span class=3D"hljs-meta">&lt;?xml v=
ersion=3D<span class=3D"hljs-string">"1.0"</span> encoding=3D<span class=3D=
"hljs-string">"utf-8"</span>?&gt;</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-tag">&lt;<span class=3D"hljs-name">network-security-con=
fig</span>&gt;</span>
    ...
    <span class=3D"hljs-tag">&lt;<span class=3D"hljs-name">domain-config</s=
pan> <span class=3D"hljs-attr">cleartextTrafficPermitted</span>=3D<span cla=
ss=3D"hljs-string">"true"</span>&gt;</span>
    <span class=3D"hljs-tag">&lt;<span class=3D"hljs-name">domain</span> <s=
pan class=3D"hljs-attr">includeSubdomains</span>=3D<span class=3D"hljs-stri=
ng">"true"</span>&gt;</span>127.0.0.1<span class=3D"hljs-tag">&lt;/<span cl=
ass=3D"hljs-name">domain</span>&gt;</span>
    <span class=3D"hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class=3D"hljs-name">domain-config</=
span>&gt;</span>
    ...
<span class=3D"hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class=3D"hljs-name">network-security-co=
nfig</span>&gt;</span>
</code></pre>
<p>Add <em>android:networkSecurityConfig=3D"@xml/network_security_config"</=
em> to <code>AndroidManifest.xml</code>:</p>
<pre><code class=3D"hljs language-xml"><span class=3D"hljs-meta">&lt;?xml v=
ersion=3D<span class=3D"hljs-string">"1.0"</span> encoding=3D<span class=3D=
"hljs-string">"utf-8"</span>?&gt;</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-tag">&lt;<span class=3D"hljs-name">manifest</span> <spa=
n class=3D"hljs-attr">...</span>&gt;</span>
    <span class=3D"hljs-tag">&lt;<span class=3D"hljs-name">uses-permission<=
/span> <span class=3D"hljs-attr">android:name</span>=3D<span class=3D"hljs-=
string">"android.permission.INTERNET"</span> /&gt;</span>
    <span class=3D"hljs-tag">&lt;<span class=3D"hljs-name">application</spa=
n>
        <span class=3D"hljs-attr">...</span>
        <span class=3D"hljs-attr">android:networkSecurityConfig</span>=3D<s=
pan class=3D"hljs-string">"@xml/network_security_config"</span>&gt;</span>
        ...
    <span class=3D"hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class=3D"hljs-name">application</sp=
an>&gt;</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class=3D"hljs-name">manifest</span>&gt;=
</span>
</code></pre>
</li>
</ol>

<h2 id=3D"initialize-the-bigo-ads-sdk">Initialize the Bigo Ads SDK</h2>
<p>Before sending any ad requests, you need to inititalize the Bigo Ads SDK=
, please do initialization like below:
The first step is to construct an <code>AdConfig</code> object by its build=
er:</p>
<pre><code class=3D"hljs language-java"><span class=3D"hljs-type">AdConfig<=
/span> <span class=3D"hljs-variable">config</span> <span class=3D"hljs-oper=
ator">=3D</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">new</span> <span class=3D"hlj=
s-title class_">AdConfig</span>.Builder()
        .setAppId(<span class=3D"hljs-string">"&lt;your-app-Id&gt;"</span>)
        .setDebug(BuildConfig.DEBUG)
        .setChannel(<span class=3D"hljs-string">"&lt;your-app-channel&gt;"<=
/span>)
        .setAge(<span class=3D"hljs-string">"&lt;your-app-user-age&gt;"</sp=
an>)
        .setGender(AdConfig.GENDER_MALE)
        .setActivatedTime(<span class=3D"hljs-string">"&lt;your-app-activat=
ed-timestamp&gt;"</span>)
        .build();
</code></pre>








































<table><thead><tr><th>AdConfig.Builder Method</th><th>Description</th><th>-=
</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>setAppId</td><td>Set up your App Id which =
could be found from the <a href=3D"https://www.bigossp.com/">BigoAds Platfo=
rm</a>.</td><td>Required</td></tr><tr><td>setDebug</td><td>Set debug mode. =
If set true, there will be more log output to help you troubleshooting duri=
ng the integration. The default value is false. <strong>Make sure to set fa=
lse before you launch your app into public officially</strong>.</td><td>Opt=
ional</td></tr><tr><td>setChannel</td><td>Set your app's distribution chann=
el. This will help us to optimize the efficiency of advertising monetizatio=
n by channel.</td><td>Optional</td></tr><tr><td>setAge</td><td>Set user's a=
ge.</td><td>Optional</td></tr><tr><td>setGender</td><td>Set user's gender. =
1:female=EF=BC=8C2:male</td><td>Optional</td></tr><tr><td>setActivatedTime<=
/td><td>Set app's activated timestamp.</td><td>Optional</td></tr></tbody></=
table>
<p>Next, call the <code>BigoAdSdk.initialize()</code> method which need to =
be done only once, and ideally at the time when app launchs. You can pass i=
n a <code>BigoAdSdk.InitListener</code> instance to receive the callback of=
 the completion of initialization. Here's an example how to do the initiali=
zation when an <code>Application</code> create:</p>
<pre><code class=3D"hljs language-java">...
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">import</span> sg.bigo.ads.BigoAdSdk;
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">import</span> sg.bigo.ads.api.AdConfig;

<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">public</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">cla=
ss</span> <span class=3D"hljs-title class_">AdApplication</span> <span clas=
s=3D"hljs-keyword">extends</span> <span class=3D"hljs-title class_">Applica=
tion</span> {
   =20
    <span class=3D"hljs-meta">@Override</span>
    <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">public</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword"=
>void</span> <span class=3D"hljs-title function_">onCreate</span><span clas=
s=3D"hljs-params">()</span> {
        ...
        <span class=3D"hljs-type">AdConfig</span> <span class=3D"hljs-varia=
ble">config</span> <span class=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span> <span class=3D"=
hljs-keyword">new</span> <span class=3D"hljs-title class_">AdConfig</span>.=
Builder()
                .setAppId(<span class=3D"hljs-string">"&lt;your-app-id&gt;"=
</span>)
                .setDebug(BuildConfig.DEBUG)
                .setChannel(<span class=3D"hljs-string">"&lt;your-app-chann=
el&gt;"</span>)
                .setAge(<span class=3D"hljs-string">"&lt;your-app-user-age&=
gt;"</span>)
                .setGender(AdConfig.GENDER_MALE)
                .setActivatedTime(<span class=3D"hljs-string">"&lt;your-app=
-activated-timestamp&gt;"</span>)
                .build();
        BigoAdSdk.initialize(<span class=3D"hljs-built_in">this</span>, con=
fig, <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">new</span> <span class=3D"hljs-title clas=
s_">BigoAdSdk</span>.InitListener() {
            <span class=3D"hljs-meta">@Override</span>
            <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">public</span> <span class=3D"hljs-=
keyword">void</span> <span class=3D"hljs-title function_">onInitialized</sp=
an><span class=3D"hljs-params">()</span> {
                <span class=3D"hljs-comment">// You can request ads now!</s=
pan>
            }
        });
    }
}
</code></pre>
<h1 id=3D"ad-formats">Ad Formats</h1>
<h2 id=3D"banner-ads">Banner Ads</h2>
<p>Banner ads occupy a spot within an app's layout(bottom etc.). They displ=
ay on screen while users are interacting with the app, and can refresh auto=
matically after a certain period of time.</p>
<h3 id=3D"load-an-ad">Load an ad</h3>
<p>Before requesting banner ads, please make sure that the Bigo Ads SDK has=
 been <a href=3D"https://www.bigossp.com/guide/sdk/android/document#initial=
ize-the-bigo-ads-sdk">initialized</a>.</p>
<p>To request an banner ad, you need to declare a <code>BannerAd</code> obj=
ect first:</p>
<pre><code class=3D"hljs language-java">BannerAd mBannerAd;
</code></pre>
<p>Then construct a <code>BannerAdRequest</code> instance and pass in the S=
lot Id and expected <a href=3D"https://www.bigossp.com/guide/sdk/android/do=
cument#banner-sizes">Banner sizes</a>.</p>
<pre><code class=3D"hljs language-java"><span class=3D"hljs-type">BannerAdR=
equest</span> <span class=3D"hljs-variable">bannerAdRequest</span> <span cl=
ass=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">new</span> <s=
pan class=3D"hljs-title class_">BannerAdRequest</span>.Builder()
                .withSlotId(<span class=3D"hljs-string">"&lt;your-slot-id&g=
t;"</span>)
                .withAdSizes(AdSize.BANNER)
                .withAge(<span class=3D"hljs-string">"&lt;your-app-user-age=
&gt;"</span>)
                .withGender(AdConfig.GENDER_MALE)
                .withActivatedTime(<span class=3D"hljs-string">"&lt;your-ap=
p-activated-timestamp&gt;"</span>)
                .build();
</code></pre>





























<table><thead><tr><th>BannerAdRequest.Builder Method</th><th>Decription</th=
></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>withSlotId</td><td>Pass in the Slot Id that re=
ferred to this ad (you can find it on <a href=3D"https://www.bigossp.com/">=
Bigo Ads platform</a>).</td></tr><tr><td>withAdSizes</td><td>Pass in the ex=
pected <a href=3D"https://www.bigossp.com/guide/sdk/android/document#banner=
-sizes">Banner sizes</a>. It's acceptable to pass in multiple standard size=
s specified by Bigo Ads at the same time.</td></tr><tr><td>withAge</td><td>=
Pass user's age.</td></tr><tr><td>withGender</td><td>Pass user's gender. 1:=
female=EF=BC=8C2:male</td></tr><tr><td>withActivatedTime</td><td>Pass app's=
 activated timestamp.</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>Next, construct a <code>BannerAdLoader</code> instance and pass in the <=
code>AdLoadListener</code> to receive callbacks from the ad request. Now, c=
all <code>loadAd()</code> method to start an ad request:</p>
<pre><code class=3D"hljs language-java"><span class=3D"hljs-type">BannerAdL=
oader</span> <span class=3D"hljs-variable">bannerAdLoader</span> <span clas=
s=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">new</span> <spa=
n class=3D"hljs-title class_">BannerAdLoader</span>.Builder().
        withAdLoadListener(<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">new</span> <span cl=
ass=3D"hljs-title class_">AdLoadListener</span>&lt;BannerAd&gt;() {
            <span class=3D"hljs-meta">@Override</span>
            <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">public</span> <span class=3D"hljs-=
keyword">void</span> <span class=3D"hljs-title function_">onError</span><sp=
an class=3D"hljs-params">(<span class=3D"hljs-meta">@NonNull</span> AdError=
 error)</span> {
                <span class=3D"hljs-comment">// There's something wrong dur=
ing ad loading</span>
            }

            <span class=3D"hljs-meta">@Override</span>
            <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">public</span> <span class=3D"hljs-=
keyword">void</span> <span class=3D"hljs-title function_">onAdLoaded</span>=
<span class=3D"hljs-params">(<span class=3D"hljs-meta">@NonNull</span> Bann=
erAd ad)</span> {
                mBannerAd =3D ad;
            }
        }).build();

bannerAdLoader.loadAd(bannerAdRequest);
</code></pre>

















<table><thead><tr><th>AdLoadListener&lt;BannerAd&gt; Callback</th><th>Descr=
iption</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>onError(AdError error)</td><td>This =
callback will be triggered when the ad request fails. Please use the <code>=
AdError.getCode()</code> and <code>AdError.getMessage()</code> Method to ch=
eck the error code and message. You can find more details in <a href=3D"htt=
ps://www.bigossp.com/guide/sdk/android/document#ad-request-error-codes">Err=
or codes</a>.</td></tr><tr><td>onAdLoaded(BannerAd ad)</td><td>This callbac=
k will be triggered if the ad request succeeds, meanwhile, an <code>BannerA=
d</code> instance will be returned.</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>Here's an example that shows how to load an banner ad in the <code>onCre=
ate()</code> method of an Activity:</p>
<pre><code class=3D"hljs language-java">...
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">import</span> sg.bigo.ads.api.AdError;
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">import</span> sg.bigo.ads.api.AdLoadListener;
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">import</span> sg.bigo.ads.api.AdSize;
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">import</span> sg.bigo.ads.api.BannerAd;
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">import</span> sg.bigo.ads.api.BannerAdLoader;
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">import</span> sg.bigo.ads.api.BannerAdRequest;

<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">public</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">cla=
ss</span> <span class=3D"hljs-title class_">MainActivity</span> <span class=
=3D"hljs-keyword">extends</span> <span class=3D"hljs-title class_">Activity=
</span> {

    BannerAd mBannerAd;

    <span class=3D"hljs-meta">@Override</span>
    <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">protected</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keywo=
rd">void</span> <span class=3D"hljs-title function_">onCreate</span><span c=
lass=3D"hljs-params">(<span class=3D"hljs-meta">@Nullable</span> Bundle sav=
edInstanceState)</span> {
        ...
        <span class=3D"hljs-type">BannerAdRequest</span> <span class=3D"hlj=
s-variable">bannerAdRequest</span> <span class=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span>=
 <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">new</span> <span class=3D"hljs-title class_">=
BannerAdRequest</span>.Builder()
                .withSlotId(<span class=3D"hljs-string">"&lt;your-slot-id&g=
t;"</span>)
