<h2 id=3D"native-ads">Native Ads</h2>
<p>Native ads are some ad assets that are presented to users via UI compone=
nts, you can design your own ad style that fits for your app, which gives a=
 good experience to your users.</p>
<h3 id=3D"load-an-ad-1">Load an ad</h3>
<p>Before requesting native ads, please make sure that the Bigo Ads SDK has=
 been <a href=3D"https://www.bigossp.com/guide/sdk/android/document#initial=
ize-the-bigo-ads-sdk">initialized</a>.</p>
<p>To request an native ad, you need to declare a <code>NativeAd</code> obj=
ect first:</p>
<pre><code class=3D"hljs language-java">NativeAd mNativeAd;
</code></pre>
<p>And then construct a <code>NativeAdRequest</code> instance and pass in t=
he Slot Id:</p>
<pre><code class=3D"hljs language-java"><span class=3D"hljs-type">NativeAdR=
equest</span> <span class=3D"hljs-variable">nativeAdRequest</span> <span cl=
ass=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">new</span> <s=
pan class=3D"hljs-title class_">NativeAdRequest</span>.Builder()
        .withSlotId(<span class=3D"hljs-string">"&lt;your-slot-id&gt;"</spa=
n>)
        .withAge(<span class=3D"hljs-string">"&lt;your-app-user-age&gt;"</s=
pan>)
        .withGender(AdConfig.GENDER_MALE)
        .withActivatedTime(<span class=3D"hljs-string">"&lt;your-app-activa=
ted-timestamp&gt;"</span>)
        .build();
</code></pre>

























