<h1 id=3D"optional-steps">Optional Steps</h1>
<h2 id=3D"user-privacy">User Privacy</h2>
<h3 id=3D"gdpr">GDPR</h3>
<p>This section is provided for compliance with the European Union's <a hre=
f=3D"https://gdpr.eu/">General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR)</a>.</p>
<p>In order to pass GDPR consent from your users, you should make use of th=
e following API to pass a consent flag to the Bigo Ads SDK:</p>
<pre><code class=3D"hljs language-java"><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">import=
</span> sg.bigo.ads.BigoAdSdk;
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">import</span> sg.bigo.ads.ConsentOptions;
...

BigoAdSdk.setUserConsent(context, ConsentOptions.GDPR, <span class=3D"hljs-=
literal">true</span>);
</code></pre>
<blockquote>
<p>A value of "<strong>true</strong>" implies the user has given consent to=
 store and process personal information and a value of "<strong>false</stro=
ng>" means the user has declined consent.</p>
<p>If the API has not been called to pass the GDPR consent, we will read th=
e local file ourselves to obtain the GDPR consent status. If there is a cal=
l, the passed GDPR consent mark prevails.</p>
</blockquote>
